{"kind":"assert","text":"Exact lifecycle selection is lost when the review verdict is written\n\nAt exact 283fe9da0a5e279f7cc465441258fbd189d6fd6f, a request with a withdrawn first promise and a current second promise is a valid projected history. The current artifact reports the second promise. `gs review --prepare --implementation \u003ccurrent-promise\u003e` resolves it successfully. Filing the same review then refuses at sequencing: its request selector matches two commitment lifecycles. The command reproduction keeps the sequence at depth22; no verdict is appended.\n\nThe cause is [BodyFields](internal/reviewguard/binding.go@283fe9da0a5e279f7cc465441258fbd189d6fd6f:462): it serializes only request IDs from Requests(), discarding the exact promise/report witness selected by Resolve. [ScopeFromVerdict](internal/reviewguard/binding.go@283fe9da0a5e279f7cc465441258fbd189d6fd6f:479) and sequencing re-resolution then see the ambiguous request again. This is an availability/contract defect, not evidence of an unauthorized merge.\n\n[Actual command reproduction](lifecycle-command_test.go) and [command output](lifecycle-command.log) show admitted withdrawal, renewed promise and current report, successful preparation, and refused filing. A [small resolver round-trip control](lifecycle-unit_test.go) isolates the information loss. Preserve an unambiguous lifecycle witness through the verdict and all its consumers; keep duplicate/uncited selector refusal and all examined-companion obligations. This correction belongs on the existing implementation commitment. Do not create another task or remove historical commitment rows to make it pass.\n\nThe earlier held/different-target omission is fixed: the four distinct command controls pass. The focused existing reviewguard, mergeplan and cmd/gs review/merge suites pass (0.320s,0.708s,134.945s respectively). The new real-command regression fails in6.741s. These are my runs; I have not repeated the author's full suite or all eight omission mutants.\n","body":{"head":"283fe9da0a5e279f7cc465441258fbd189d6fd6f","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3088e19d6b73f3603197ca7b1dca3d383d4d8085, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9694e6b1b71c84077dd96da542c1e8db678c63f9 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01ab55ec50e015756b4e4e1c274259f118956c9f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02a7302bf06f4f95ea67698d571fd7470055d448, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02a980f84e17c4f9b9e5dc91e01e963a2f39c53d and 88 more"}}